    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7702A\n\nSPONSOR: MARCHIONE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the general municipal law, in relation\nto authorizing all school districts to establish reserve funds\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 6-n of the general municipal law by providing\nthat any school district may establish insurance reserve funds in\ncompliance with section 6-n and provisions in the education law. It\nadditionally removes previous references to school districts that had\nbeen specifically authorized to do so. The provisions also include a\nlimit on funds reserved to be determined by an independent actuary.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law allows municipal corporations to self-insure to provide\nhealth insurance to their employees, officers, and retirees. Section 6-n\nof the general municipal law specifically does so by allowing these\nmunicipal corporations to establish and make expenditures from insurance\nreserve funds, but exempts accident and health insurance from these\nprovisions.\n\nPrevious chapters authorized specific school districts to use their\ninsurance reserve funds for expenses related to health and accident\ninsurance as defined by paragraph three of subsection (a) of section one\nthousand one hundred thirteen of the insurance law. In the era of the\ntax cap, several school districts have opted to adopt self-insurance to\nmanage rising healthcare costs, and for these districts, insurance\nreserve funds are necessary to maintain their self-insurance programs.\nThese districts have requested several bills currently before the legis-\nlature that would allow their individual school district to do so, but\nthe policy of the State should be aimed at allowing all school districts\nthis degree of flexibility. This bill offers exactly that by expanding\nthe authorization to any school district that wishes to create or use an\ninsurance reserve fund for health self-insurance.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill, but similar to bills introduced for individual school\ndistricts before.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of July next succeeding the date\non which it shall have become law.\n",
